ot rewind the conversation itself. The conversation history and context remain intact after calling `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewindFiles()`}),` (TypeScript) or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewind_files()`}),` (Python).`]})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`When you rewind to a checkpoint, Claude Code deletes the files it created and restores the files it modified to their content at that point. Claude Code skips a tracked path that is a symlink, hard link, or other non-regular file. It also skips a tracked file whose parent directory no longer resolves to its checkpoint-time location, or whose backup it can’t read safely. `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/agent-sdk/typescript#rewindfilesresult`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`RewindFilesResult`})}),` counts every skipped path in its `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`skippedLinks`}),` field. Skipping requires Claude Code v2.1.216 or later; before v2.1.216, a rewind wrote and deleted through links at tracked paths.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`implement-checkpointing`,children:`Implement checkpointing`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To use file checkpointing, enable it in your options, capture checkpoint UUIDs from the response stream, then call `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewindFiles()`}),` (TypeScript) or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewind_files()`}),` (Python) when you need to restore.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The examples in this section use the prompt “Refactor the authentication module”. Run them in a project that contains an authentication module, or change the prompt to name files that exist in your project, so you can watch files change and see the rewind restore them.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`This example enables checkpointing, captures the checkpoint UUID and session ID from the response stream, then resumes the session later to rewind files. The example’s numbered comments match the steps that follow.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(CodeG