oves the agent’s file edits without a prompt. For more information, see `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/agent-sdk/permissions#permission-modes`,children:`Permission modes`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(Step,{title:`Capture checkpoint UUID and session ID`,children:[_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`With the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`replay-user-messages`}),` option set, each user message in the response stream has a UUID that serves as a checkpoint.`]}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`For most use cases, capture the first user message UUID (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`message.uuid`}),`); rewinding to it restores the tracked files to their original state. To store multiple checkpoints and rewind to intermediate states, see `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#multiple-restore-points`,children:`Multiple restore points`}),`.`]}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Capturing the session ID (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`message.session_id`}),`) is optional; you only need it if you want to rewind later, after the stream completes. If you’re calling `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewindFiles()`}),` immediately while still processing messages (as the example in `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#checkpoint-before-risky-operations`,children:`Checkpoint before risky operations`}),` does), you can skip capturing the session ID.`]})]}),_jsxs(Step,{title:`Rewind files`,children:[_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To rewind after the stream completes, resume the session with an empty prompt and call `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewind_files()`}),` (Python) or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rewindFiles()`}),` (TypeScript) with your checkpoint UUID. Enable checkpointing on the resumed session’s options too, and call rewind from inside the response loop. You can also rewind during the stream. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#checkpoint-before-risky-operations`,children:`Checkpoint before risky operations`}),` for that pattern.`]}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If you capture the session ID and checkpoint ID, you can also rewind from the CLI. This command requires the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude`}),` executable, which comes from `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/setup`,children:`installing Claude Code`}),`. The SDK enables checkpointing for you, but when you run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude -p`}),` directly you must set the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_SDK_FILE_CHECKPOINTING`}),` environment variable:`]}),_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`1`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`1`,children:[_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#9CDCFE`},children:`CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_SDK_FILE_CHECKPOINTING`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`=`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`true`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:` claude`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0550AE`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#569CD6`},children:` -p`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0550AE`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#569CD6`},children:` --resume`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` \u003c`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`session-i`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`d`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`\u003e`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0550AE`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#569CD6`},children:` --rewind-files`}),_jsx(_components.sp